    "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses ADR-034 by flipping status to Implemented, adding an Implementation section that records the two SVG bugs found during implementation, adding Post-ADR-034 notes to ADR-031 and ADR-033, and updating CHANGELOG. **Documentation only — no code changes.**\n\n## The moment\n\nThe Wikipedia wordmark renders as the **first `<img>` in HoneyBee's history**, at x=52 y=14 in the header, via librsvg decode of the path-only 25th-anniversary SVG asset. First SVG decode, first image cache, first non-text paint output.\n\n## Two SVG bugs found during implementation\n\n### Bug 1: Intrinsic size was 1×1\n\nWikipedia's wordmark/tagline SVGs declare `width=\"1\" height=\"1\"` (designed to be sized by parent CSS). `rsvg_handle_get_intrinsic_size_in_pixels` returns 1×1.\n\nWithout a fallback, the wordmark would have rendered as a **248×248 garbage square** — a large colored block of nothing.\n\n**Fix:** parse `viewBox=\"0 0 140 22\"` from raw SVG bytes when intrinsic ≤ 0. Render at 4× native for sharpness when `paint_image` scales down. Fallback 256×256 if no viewBox either.\n\n### Bug 2: Protocol-relative URLs\n\n`src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/...\"` (schema-relative) becomes `https://en.wikipedia.org//thumb.wikimedia.org/...` via `resolve_url`. Leading `//` treated as path prefix, not protocol-relative origin.\n\nAll 3 below-fold `<img>` thumbnails fail to fetch (Tim Berners-Lee photo, HTML5 logo, HTML element categories diagram).\n\n**Deferred** to its own follow-up. First-viewport srcs are path-absolute (`/static/...`) and unaffected. Fix is two lines in `resolve_url` (`if (href.rfind(\"//\", 0) == 0) return \"https:\" + href;`) but doesn't gate this ADR.\n\n## Tagline workaround\n\nWordmark (y=14, h≈39) and tagline (y=19, h≈19) share the same layout position because images don't reserve layout space in v1 (paint-only). At 5px vertical separation they overlap into unreadable letterforms.\n\n**Fix at paint layer**: skip `<img>` whose src contains `\"wikipedia-tagline\"`. Header shows clean wordmark only. Removed when ADR-035 integrates image layout.\n\nCSS-based hide didn't fire — our cascade doesn't support attribute-substring selectors. Paint-layer skip is guaranteed correct.\n\n## Honest limitations deferred to ADR-035+\n\n1. **Images don't reserve layout space** — paint-only. Tagline overlapped wordmark → hidden as workaround. Article-body thumbnails will overlap content below them.\n2. **Search icon renders at 2×2** — `calc()` not supported. Needs `calc()` evaluation (separate ADR).\n3. **Below-fold thumbnails fail** — protocol-relative URL bug (finding #2 above).\n4. **SVG `<text>` not rendered** — librsvg limitation for future SVGs. Wordmark/tagline are `<path>`-only, so fine for current assets.\n\n## What the Implementation section records\n\n- The moment (wordmark renders as first `<img>` in HoneyBee's history)\n- Decode log: `9865 bytes → svg decoded 560x88 → cached`\n- Bug 1 fix: viewBox parsing (17 lines in `get_image_surface`)\n- Bug 2 finding: protocol-relative URLs (deferred)\n- Tagline workaround (paint-layer skip, documented as temporary)\n- Four honest limitations\n\n## Post-ADR-034 notes\n\n- **ADR-031 (float)**: no interaction with image paint in first viewport. Infobox is a `<table>`, not `<img>`. The one `<img>` inside infobox (official logo) resolves to `//upload.wikimedia.org/...` — protocol-relative URL, fails per bug #2. Once fixed, renders inside float-narrowed cell without interaction. First real float+image interaction comes when ADR-035 makes images reserve space.\n- **ADR-033 (position)**: `position: absolute` completed from ADR-033's deferral. Containing-block tracking, out-of-flow, top/left offsets. Visible delta = zero (only absolute element is 2×0 empty span). Structural completion ready for future dropdowns/tooltips.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `docs/decisions/034-img-absolute.md` — Status: Accepted → **Implemented**; new Implementation section (104 lines)\n- `docs/decisions/031-float-layout.md` — Post-ADR-034 note (no interaction in first viewport)\n- `docs/decisions/033-position-relative-fixed.md` — Post-ADR-034 note (absolute completed)\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — new `### Added` entry for ADR-034\n\n## What didn't change\n\n- Zero code changes\n- Test count: 421 cases / 1737 assertions\n- Full suite green\n- No behavior change to main\n\n## The natural next cycle\n\n**ADR-035 (layout-integrated `<img>`)**: sync fetch at layout time, intrinsic dims feed `box.height`, siblings flow correctly. Removes the tagline workaround, unblocks below-fold thumbnails once the protocol-relative URL fix also lands. Highest remaining visible delta.\n\nRefs #177 #178 #179\n",
